  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Beer depletions stop falling in FY28 as Pacifico, Victoria and Modelo Chelada keep taking share and flagship Modelo Especial/Corona Extra flatten; enterprise revenue dips ~1.5% in FY27 (flat organic plus the Wine Divestitures lap) then recovers to 2-3%. Comparable operating margin settles in the guided 32-33% band (adj. EBITDA ~38%) as 2025 restructuring savings land, and capex falls from ~9% of sales to ~5.5% once the Mexican brewery build completes, lifting owner FCF from ~$1.9B to ~$2.4B by FY31.",
    "bull": "The Hispanic-consumer soft patch proves cyclical (immigration-enforcement fear and value-seeking ease), the April 2026 malt-beverage tariff carve-out holds, and the new CEO sharpens price-pack architecture and W&S premiumisation. Beer returns to 4-5% growth, margins reach ~39.5% adj. EBITDA, and the $4.0B buyback compounds per-share value from a ~10x earnings base.",
    "bear": "The flagship decline is structural rather than cyclical: Modelo Especial and Corona Extra keep losing volume to moderation, spirits/RTDs and cannabis while the core demographic stays under pressure, and smaller brands are too small to offset. Revenue falls two years running, fixed-cost deleverage and 50% aluminum tariffs hold adj. EBITDA at ~35%, leverage pins near 3.0x, and trade policy towards Mexico remains a recurring tail."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Mature staples-like cash generator priced as if the flagship decline is permanent. Owner FCF on a fully expensed SBC basis (SBC is small, ~0.85% of sales), unlevered flows at a 7.5% USD WACC, NCI deducted once, terminal capped at 13-17x to stop Gordon from paying a perpetuity multiple a buyer need not grant. The swing factors are beer volume and the capex fade, not accounting.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Modelo Especial / Corona Extra depletion declines prove structural (base assumes they flatten by FY28)",
      "US trade policy on Mexican imports: malt-beverage tariff carve-out reversed, or aluminum tariffs raised further",
      "Capex fails to fade to ~5.5% of sales (another capacity round) - each 1pp of sales is ~$90M/yr of FCF",
      "Cash tax rises faster than the 17%->20% ramp as the DTA shelter runs off",
      "Leverage ~3.0x net debt/EBITDA: equity is ~65% of EV so every 10% move in EV is ~15% per share",
      "Q2 FY27 results (2026-10-06) may reset FY27 guidance; this build is anchored to the July 2026 guide"
    ]
  },
