    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (dcf-methods routing row 2: US consumer operating company with moderate cyclicality). STZ is a producer/importer of Mexican beer plus a small wine & spirits segment - not a bank/REIT/holdco/LIC; FCF is a real operating stream. First valuation of STZ (no MEMORY entry, no prior DCF). FY0 = FY2026 (ended 2026-02-28): revenue $9,139.0M (Beer ~$8.3B, W&S ~$0.82B after the 2025 Wine Divestitures). Adjusted EBITDA FY26 = op income 2,721.4 + D&A 420.0 + asset impairment 109.8 + loss on sale 31.9 + SBC 67.7 = $3,350.8M (36.7%). Year-1 (FY27) margin set at 36.5% to absorb restructuring cash costs and to reconcile with guidance: guided FCF $1.6-1.7B (OCF $2.4-2.5B less ~$0.8B capex) + ~$270M after-tax interest - $77M SBC implies ~$1.84B unlevered owner FCF; the component build gives ~$1.92B. Revenue path starts at -1.5% for FY27: guided organic (1)% to +1% plus the Q1 lap of the 2025 Wine Divestitures (Q1 FY27 net sales -3.3% YoY) - the shrinking W&S mix is not extrapolated as a flat company growth rate. Capex ~9.2% FY27 (beer ~$800M Mexican brewery capacity) glides to ~5.5% (just above D&A ~5%) once Nava/Obregon expansion completes. Cash tax: FY26 taxes paid were only $173.6M (~7% of pretax) on DTA unwind from the intra-entity IP transfer and OB3 bonus depreciation; modelled at 17% FY27 rising to 20% by FY30 - the shelter is NOT perpetuated into the terminal year. Canopy Growth: FY24-FY25 impairments ($511.8M equity losses FY24, $76.1M FY25 exchangeable-share write-down) and the FY25 $2.8B W&S goodwill impairment are non-cash and non-recurring; excluded from run-rate. Exchangeable shares carried at $21.2M added in the bridge. Net debt = short-term borrowings 336.3 + current LTD 1,102.6 + LTD 9,094.9 - cash 96.6 = $10,437.2M at 2026-05-31, plus $100.0M of buybacks executed between 1 June and 26 June 2026 (debt-funded) so net debt matches the 26 June share count -> $10,537.2M. Buybacks: $924.1M FY26, $223.8M Q1 FY27 - the flat count is funded by real repurchases ($2.75B left on the $4.0B authorization). Q2 FY27 results due 2026-10-06 after close: re-anchor FY27 growth/margin then.",
